\n$$\n\nwhere $4$ is a perfect square. So, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{12} =\\sqrt{4 \\cdot 3}= \\sqrt{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 2\\sqrt{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124295 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4744" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124295 #edb/ref 1071 "Write $3 \\sqrt{5}$ as the square root of a single number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124295 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "204328e4-810f-591e-a085-bb9cdadca875" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124295 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that\n\n$$\n3 = \\sqrt{9}\n$$\n\nSo, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{9}\\cdot\\sqrt{5}= \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{45}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124296 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124296 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\sqrt[3]{2}\\cdot\\sqrt[3]{3}$ as the cube root of a single number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c797a57-00a8-57b9-af30-655e8952c4c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124296 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{2}\\cdot\\sqrt[3]{3}= \\sqrt[3]{2\\cdot 3} = \\sqrt[3]{6}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1039 "Separating a Square Root Into a Product of Two Square Roots" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124481 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "202575c6-7672-5387-a5ae-762bef520add" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124482 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124482 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124482 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing a Product of Two Square Roots as a Single